  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Sudan Kosti Hub Operations, White Nile State.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The significant action point the Bishops and the Caritas Sudan team are aiming at is to establish and equip a coordination office in Kosti, White Nile, from where to reconvene its activities and plan on the next course of actions regarding programming with a focus on emergency response working closely with its strategic partners and the local authorities.

This process also enhances the workforce&apos;s capacity to undertake the tasks and roles. As a way of achieving this, the recruitment process was resumed with the support of CAFOD and some changes to the posts given the situation in the country. Recruiting a Finance Assistant and a finance consultant to establish the necessary financial and accounting systems have been done, including an experienced Emergency Response Officer (ERO) to guide emergency and humanitarian responses in the current humanitarian responses. Given the current humanitarian situation in the country, the need for a Programme Officer - Emergency Response was seen to be vital. Therefore, the post of Social Cohesion Officer was put on hold. The Kosti pastoral region has provided space to house the Caritas offices, which requires repairs and equipping. If needed, the Khartoum Archbishop has offered additional office space in Wad Medani to coordinate activities for the IDPs in Al Jazira state. Getting the Kosti coordination office up and running will require financial support, as highlighted in the budget in the attached Excel sheet</narrative>
  </description>
